Revision history for Perl extension CGI-PSGI-Minimum

{{$NEXT}}

    - header()/psgi_header() now interpret arguments like CGI.pm
      (key normalization, aliases, arbitrary headers, -cookie, -target,
      -expires, -attachment, -p3p, -nph). Previously these croaked.
    - redirect()/psgi_redirect() now interpret arguments like CGI.pm
      (-location/-uri/-url, -status (default "302 Found"), -target,
      -cookie, -nph, and arbitrary headers).
    - Add cache() (CGI.pm compatible; cache(1) means "do NOT cache").
    - Add has_header(), as_cgi_header() and as_cgi_response() to serialize
      the stored response in CGI style (for CGI/FastCGI drivers and tests).
    - Guard against HTTP response splitting (CWE-113) when storing and
      when serializing headers.
    - Add $PARAM_UTF8 / declare_param_utf8, equivalent of CGI.pm's -utf8 (param() decoding)
    - CGI.pm compatibility: param() setter ignores undef values and leaves the parameter untouched when no defined value is given

    - original version

